{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 17]], "date-time": "2026-08-17T14:56:37Z", "timestamp": 1786978597383, "version": "build-2736575974"}, "reference-count": 59, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "1", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 1, 14]], "date-time": "2024-01-14T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1705190400000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["acsess.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["The Plant Genome"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2024, 3]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Spot blotch caused by\n                    <jats:italic>Bipolaris sorokiniana</jats:italic>\n                    ((Sacc.) Shoemaker) (teleomorph:\n                    <jats:italic>Cochliobolus sativus</jats:italic>\n                    [Ito and Kuribayashi] Drechsler ex Dastur) is an economically important disease of warm and humid regions. The present study focused on identifying resistant genotypes and single\u2010nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) markers associated with spot blotch resistance in a panel of 174 bread spring wheat lines using field screening and genome\u2010wide association mapping strategies. Field experiments were conducted in Agua Fria, Mexico, during the 2019\u20132020 and 2020\u20132021 cropping seasons. A wide range of phenotypic variation was observed among genotypes tested during both years. Twenty SNP markers showed significant association with spot blotch resistance on 15 chromosomes, namely, 1A, 1B, 2A, 2B, 2D, 3A, 3B, 4B, 4D, 5A, 5B, 6A, 6B, 7A, and 7B. Of these, two consistently significant SNPs on 5A, TA003225\u20100566 and TA003225\u20101427, may represent a new resistance quantitative trait loci. Further, in the proximity of\n                    <jats:italic>Tsn1</jats:italic>\n                    on 5B, AX\u201094435238 was the most stable and consistent in both years. The identified genomic regions could be deployed to develop spot blotch\u2010resistant genotypes, particularly in the spot blotch\u2010vulnerable wheat growing areas.\n                  </jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1002/tpg2.20425", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 1, 15]], "date-time": "2024-01-15T05:18:13Z", "timestamp": 1705295893000}, "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1002/crossmark_policy", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 6, "title": ["Genome\u2010wide association mapping for field spot blotch resistance in South Asian spring wheat genotypes"], "prefix": "10.1002", "volume": "17", "author": [{"given": "Umesh", "family": "Kamble", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "ICAR\u2010Indian Institute of Wheat and Barley Research  Karnal Haryana India"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Xinyao", "family": "He", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "International Maize and Wheat Improvement Centre (CIMMYT) Apedo  Mexico City Mexico"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8040-5563", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Sudhir", "family": "Navathe", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Agharkar Research Institute  Pune India"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Manjeet", "family": "Kumar", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "ICAR\u2010Indian Agricultural Research Institute  New Delhi India"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Madhu", "family": "Patial", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "ICAR\u2010Indian Agricultural Research Institute  New Delhi India"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Muhammad Rezaul", "family": "Kabir", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Bangladesh Wheat and Maize Research Institute (BWMRI)  